    {
      "id": "p0162-b005",
      "kind": "paragraph",
      "source": {
        "text": "As with several other characters in Undertale, Onionsan's gender is meant to be unclear. As such, Onionsan usually uses the polite, somewhat gender neutral Japanese pronoun watashi. On other occasions, Onionsan simply says \"Onionsan\" instead of using a pronoun, which lends the character even more of a childish vibe.",
        "raw": "As with several other characters in Undertale, Onionsan's gender is meant\nto be unclear. As such, Onionsan usually uses the polite, somewhat gender\nneutral Japanese pronoun watashi. On other occasions, Onionsan simply says\n\"Onionsan\" instead of using a pronoun, which lends the character even more of\na childish vibe.",
        "status": "corrected",
        "languages": [
          "en"
        ],
        "bbox": [
          0.29531984,
          0.46566429,
          0.90589625,
          0.54996429
        ],
        "mask_bbox": [
          0.29232069,
          0.46495,
          0.91265705,
          0.55103571
        ],
        "line_ids": [
          25,
          26,
          27,
          28,
          29
        ]
      },
      "translation": {
        "text": "和 Undertale 的其他几个角色一样，Onionsan 的性别有意保持模糊。因此，其日语通常采用礼貌、相对中性的第一人称 watashi（我）。有时又不用代词，直接以“Onionsan”自称，令角色更显孩子气。",
        "status": "draft",
        "spans": [
